# WIRING_REGISTER.md IS GENERATED, AND GIT MUST NOT TRY TO MERGE IT.
#
# This file has been silently mis-merged repeatedly, always the same way — git
# found two adjacent blocks it could interleave, kept both sides, and produced a
# file that looked plausible and was wrong. The worst of them left `table:leads`
# present twice with contradictory scores, one copy still quoting a "respond
# within 24 hours" promise the code had already stopped making. A register that
# asserts a fixed defect is still live is worse than no register.
#
# ── WHAT THIS SETTING USED TO BE, AND WHY IT CHANGED ─────────────────────────
#
# It was `-merge`: refuse to merge, raise a conflict, and let a human run the
# generator. The reasoning was written down here — "a conflict is what makes
# somebody run it."
#
# IT DOES NOT. The file was hand-merged TWICE THIS WEEK with `-merge` in place.
# The conflict arrives, somebody picks a side or splices the two, and a register
# describing neither branch lands on main. A rule that depends on the person
# holding the conflict doing the right thing fails at exactly the moment it
# matters — late in the day, with four branches in flight.
#
# So the conflict is REMOVED rather than relied upon. `merge=regen` runs
# scripts/wiring/merge-driver.mjs, which runs the generator. For a generated
# file there is nothing to reconcile: every byte comes from the code plus
# scripts/wiring/annotations.mjs.
#
# ── THE DRIVER IS NOT AUTOMATIC, AND CANNOT BE ──────────────────────────────
#
# Git will not run a driver a repository merely asks for: `.gitattributes` is
# committed and executing code from it would make cloning a repo dangerous. Each
# checkout registers it once —
#
#     npm run setup          (or: bash scripts/setup-repo.sh)
#
# — and until somebody does, git falls back to its ORDINARY TEXTUAL MERGE, which
# is the interleaving this file exists to prevent. That gap is why the CI
# self-heal on main (.github/workflows/ci.yml) exists as well: belt and braces,
# because the belt is per-clone and cannot be enforced from here.
#
# This is the same class as the locale-JSON rule in CLAUDE.md ("resolving a
# locale conflict is not concatenation"), which came out of two production
# outages with the same cause. Here the fix can be structural, because unlike
# en.json this file has a generator.
WIRING_REGISTER.md merge=regen linguist-generated=true
